        "math_academy_id": "q-317847",
        "problem": "Determine $AB$ given that \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | $4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $0$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
        "worked_solution": "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{\u2713}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute the unknown elements of $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & \u2217\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,5=2\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & [\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}], &  & \\,7=4\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
